<title>USA: Credit Lyonnais ups Venezuela in stock portfolio.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais ups Venezuela in stock portfolio.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Lyonnais raised Venezuela's weighting to five from three percent in a model portfolio of Latin American stocks.</p>
<p>In a report issued late on Friday, analyst Francois Gour cited dropping inflation, upcoming privatizations, the pending invasion of foreign brokers and market trades at a discount to the region among reasons for the upgrade.</p>
<p>Venezuelan stocks have more of an upside than Brady bonds, she said.</p>
<p>-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730</p>
</text>
